WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.684
Clear speaking is not simply speaking slowly.

00:00:02.684 --> 00:00:05.189
It means making your ideas easy to follow.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:11.154
Use one main idea per sentence, define unfamiliar terms, and tell your listener where
you are going.

00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:15.270
A strong opening gives both a reason to care and a map of the speech.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.192
A pause gives an important idea room to land.

00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:23.851
Vary your emphasis to reflect meaning rather than repeating the same pattern.

00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:26.816
Your ideal pace depends on the audience and task.

00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:31.595
A word count estimate is only a planning aid, not a score for speaking quality.

00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:35.465
Record a short explanation and listen back.

00:00:35.465 --> 00:00:41.115
Choose one improvement: a clearer opening, fewer fillers, or a pause after your main
claim.

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:43.350
Repeat the same passage and compare.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.461
This makes improvement observable.

00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:50.180
The practice room lets you record and download a take without publishing it.
